G5043.def:
**τέκνον**, -ου, τό
(τίκτω), [in LXX chiefly for בֵּן, also for יֶלֶד, etc. ;]
that which is begotten, born (cf. Scottish _bairn_), **a child** of either sex: [[Mrk.13.12|Mrk.13:12]], [[Luk.1.7|Luk.1:7]], [[Act.7.5|Act.7:5]]; pl., [[Mat.7.11|Mat.7:11]], [[Mrk.7.27|Mrk.7:27]], [[Luk.1.17|Luk.1:17]], [[Eph.6.1|Eph.6:1]], al.; τέκνα ἐπαγγελίας, [[Rom.9.8|Rom.9:8]] τ. τῆς σαρκός, ib.; in a wider sense (as Heb. בָּנִים), of posterity, [[Mat.2.18|Mat.2:18]], [[Luk.3.8|Luk.3:8]], al.; specif., of a male child, [[Mat.21.28|Mat.21:28]], [[Act.21.21|Act.21:21]], a,l.; in voc. as a form of kindly address from an elder to a junior or from a teacher to a disciple, [[Mat.9.2; 21.28|Mat.9:2 21:28]], [[Mrk.2.5|Mrk.2:5]], [[Luk.2.48|Luk.2:48]]; τ. μου (= cl. τ. μοι; see Bl., §37, 5), [[Gal.4.19|Gal.4:19]] (τεκνία, WH, txt.), [[2Ti.2.1|2Ti.2:1]] Metaphorical,
(a) **of disciples **(apart from direct address, see supr.): Phm 10, [[1Ti.1.2|1Ti.1:2]], [[Tit.1.4|Tit.1:4]], [[3Jn.4|3Jo.4]];
(b) with reference to the Fatherhood of God (see: πατήρ, γεννάω), τέκνα τ. θεοῦ (cf. [[Isa.30.1|Isa.30:1]], [[Wis.16.21|Wis.16:21]]): [[Rom.8.16|Rom.8:16]], [[Eph.5.1|Eph.5:1]], [[Php.2.15|Php.2:15]]; and esp. in Johannine bks. (cf. Westc, _Epp. Jo._, 94, 120), [[Jhn.1.12|Jhn.1:12]], [[1Jn.3.1|1Jn.3:1]] al.;
(with) **of those who imitate others and are therefore regarded as the spiritual offspring of their exemplars**: [[Mat.3.9|Mat.3:9]], [[Luk.3.8|Luk.3:8]], [[Jhn.8.39|Jhn.8:39]], [[Rom.9.7|Rom.9:7]], [[1Pe.3.6|1Pe.3:6]]; τ. διαβόλου, [[1Jn.3.10|1Jn.3:10]]
(d) as in Heb. (LXX, [[Jol.2.23|Jol.2:23]], [[Psa.149.2|Psa.149:2]], [[1Ma.1.38|1Ma.1:38]]), of the inhabitants of a city: [[Mat.23.37|Mat.23:37]], [[Luk.13.34; 19.44|Luk.13:34 19:44]], [[Gal.4.25|Gal.4:25]];
(e) with an adjectival genitive, frequently rendering a Heb. expression, adopted from LXX or formed on the analogy of its language, but sometimes with parallels in Gk. writers (see Deiss., _BS_, 161ff.): τέκνα φωτός, [[Eph.5.8|Eph.5:8]] τ. ὑπακοῆς, [[1Pe.1.14|1Pe.1:14]] κατάρας, [[2Pe.2.14|2Pe.2:14]] ὀργῆς, [[Eph.2.3|Eph.2:3]]
_SYN._: see: παῖς. (AS)
